{"name":"Honolulu","hex":"#96cbf1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Honolulu","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A port in Oahu Island; the capital and largest city of Hawaii, United States and the county seat of Honolulu County, Hawaii. Official name: City and County of Honolulu"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Honolulu"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honolulu","blocks":[{"text":"Honolulu is the capital and most populous city of the U.S. state of Hawaii, located in the Pacific Ocean. It is the county seat of the consolidated City and County of Honolulu, situated along the southeast coast of the island of Oʻahu. The population of Honolulu was 350,964 at the 2020 census, dropping to an estimated 341,868 by 2025. The Urban Honolulu metropolitan area had an estimated population of just under 1 million residents in 2024 and is the 56th-largest metropolitan area in the nation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/2022_Views_from_Diamond_Head_02.jpg/330px-2022_Views_from_Diamond_Head_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honolulu","wikidata":"Q18094"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Iolani_Palace_dressed_up_%2823715379385%29.jpg/500px-Iolani_Palace_dressed_up_%2823715379385%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Iolani_Palace_dressed_up_%2823715379385%29.jpg/1280px-Iolani_Palace_dressed_up_%2823715379385%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Iolani_Palace_dressed_up_%2823715379385%29.jpg/500px-Iolani_Palace_dressed_up_%2823715379385%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIolani